{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"747916376987140289","content":"So when a DM sees this.  So Hampstead has surgery as an option for some items (The heart and the Aberrant Amber are two examples)\n\nSo there is a risk of when you get surgery done, you just die (and then have to be rebuilt, just the way we like or Frankenstein's Monsters here).  So I wanted something similar to old school system shock, but simplified to use a d20 and adjusted for the stats that are more common in 5e, namely 5e is typically higher)\n\n```If someone goes under the knife for serious surgery in Hampstead, They must roll a d20 to see if they survive the procedure.  The roll cannot be modified, nor can advantage or disadvantage be applied.  The number they must roll above (not equal to) is 21-[con score].  If they fail this roll, they die, and must be rebuilt as per  the Hampstead rules for being brought back.```","created_at":"2021-06-19T17:33:46.232000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"855862940719775754","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
